      "math_academy_id": "q-218363",
      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "Let $A=R,$ and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x$ and $y$ both lie in the exterior of a circle of radius $3$ centered at $O.$ Express $R$ using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\nR=\\{{{field-1}}\\in {{field-2}}\\,:\\,{{field-3}}\\}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a\\,R\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\in R$\n\n- $a\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}$ such that ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>{3}^{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14267010/assets/28124fc92a4c5abaec7501ee3f252f16b31d1c73a1c1b1b174979d672ada799a.png)\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>9\\}\n$$",
